CLIF 1.0
namespace: clarion
clan: game-shard
source-language: en-US
target-language: zh-CN
title: "Emberveil: dialogue, skills, items and tutorial strings"
info: "Emberveil is a story-driven fantasy RPG. Ash, a fire-blooded orphan, and Flint, a plain-spoken forgehand, travel a valley being swallowed by an unnatural frost. Audience: players on PC and console. Strings appear in voiced dialogue, skill and item UI, tutorial cards and cutscene subtitles."
standard: "Translate the name 'Ash' semantically as 余烬, never 艾什, 艾许 or 阿什. Translate the name 'Flint' phonetically as 弗林特, never 燧石 or 打火石. Render the factions Emberborn and Frostward as 焰裔 and 霜卫. Keep engine placeholders such as {damage} and {playerName} and ICU MessageFormat syntax intact. Use one space between Han text and Latin letters or digits, and fullwidth punctuation inside Han sentences. Prefer compact renderings for skill and item names that must fit their width budgets."
dependency: ["game-shard-terms.zh-CN.clif"]

[dialog.ash-and-flint]
context: "Voiced dialogue between Ash, a fire-blooded orphan, and Flint, a plain-spoken forgehand, in Chapter One. Each line is acted; keep the two registers distinct."
type: dialogue

<ash-greets-flint>
source: "Flint, you still owe me a proper blade."
target: "弗林特，你还欠我一把像样的刀。"
status: final
emotion: [playful]
context: "Ash teases Flint at the forge door; friendly, not hostile."

<flint-replies-ash>
source: "Ash, you could not hold a whetstone straight if the forge froze over."
target: "余烬，就算熔炉整个冻住，你也磨不直一块磨刀石。"
status: final
emotion: [playful, rude]
context: "Flint answers with affection disguised as an insult."

<ash-fearful>
source: "Flint, the frost is moving. I saw it breathe."
target: "弗林特，霜寒在移动。我看到它在呼吸。"
status: final
emotion: [fearful]
context: "Ash reports the unnatural cold at the palisade; she is genuinely afraid."

<flint-angry>
source: "You lit that spark, Ash, and now the whole valley pays for it."
target: "是你点燃了那簇火星，余烬，如今整座山谷都在为它付出代价。"
status: final
emotion: [angry]
context: "Flint blames Ash for the spreading fire; real anger, not banter."

<flint-calls-ash>
source: "Ash! Get away from the wall — it is coming through!"
target: "余烬！离墙远点——它要穿墙而入了！"
status: final
emotion: [urgent, fearful]
context: "Flint shouts a warning as the frost breaches the palisade."

<ash-grateful>
source: "Flint, you forged me a name when no one else would. Thank you."
target: "弗林特，在没有人愿意的时候，是你为我铸下了一个名字。谢谢你。"
status: final
emotion: [grateful]
context: "Ash thanks Flint for taking her in; the single soft beat in the scene."

<flint-polite-threat>
source: "You are, of course, welcome to try again. I will even hold the door for you."
target: "当然，欢迎你再试一次。我甚至可以帮你扶着门。"
status: final
emotion: [polite]
context: "Flint speaks to a rival who just failed to cheat him. The words are courteous but the intent is a threat: surface meaning polite, subtext menacing."

[monologue.ash]
context: "Ash's interior voice, heard during quiet story beats. Register is more formal and image-driven than her spoken lines."
type: monologue

<monologue-ash-fire>
source: "The fire in my chest has a memory of its own. It knows the cold before the cold arrives, and it is afraid."
target: "我胸中的火自有记忆。霜寒未至，它便已察觉，并且感到恐惧。"
status: final
emotion: [anxious]
context: "Ash reasons through the fire-spirit's dread; literary and slower than her speech."

<monologue-ash-name>
source: "Flint says a name is a handle, not a mirror. But a name can still be a promise you make to yourself."
target: "弗林特说，名字是把手，不是镜子。可名字仍可以是你对自己许下的一个承诺。"
status: final
emotion: [calm, hopeful]
context: "Ash reflects on the weight of the name she chose."

[skills.items]
context: "Skill-bar and inventory strings. Skill and item names must fit the width budget shown on the hotbar and in the bag grid."

<skill-ember-burst>
source: "Ember Burst"
target: "焰爆"
type: noun-phrase
status: final
max-width: 6
context: "Fire skill on the hotbar; keep within the 6-cell slot."

<skill-frost-whip>
source: "Frost Whip"
target: "霜鞭"
type: noun-phrase
status: final
max-width: 6
context: "Ice skill on the hotbar; keep within the 6-cell slot."

<skill-cinder-sidestep>
source: "Cinder Sidestep"
target: "烬避"
type: noun-phrase
status: final
max-width: 6
context: "Mobility skill on the hotbar; keep within the 6-cell slot."

<skill-thorn-snare>
source: "Thorn Snare"
target: "棘缚"
type: noun-phrase
status: final
max-width: 6
context: "Crowd-control skill on the hotbar; keep within the 6-cell slot."

<item-emberbloom-tonic>
source: "Emberbloom Tonic"
target: "烬花剂"
type: noun-phrase
status: final
max-width: 8
context: "Consumable in the bag grid; keep within the 8-cell slot."

<item-axe-pun-desc>
source: "This greataxe is a real splitting headache — swing once and the argument is over."
target: "这柄巨斧真的让人头痛欲裂——一挥之下，争论便告终结。"
type: description
status: final
context: "Inventory flavor text for the greataxe 'Splitting Headache'. The phrase is a pun that must be recreated in Chinese, not translated literally."

[tutorial.system]
context: "Tutorial cards, system prompts and combat log strings shown on screen during the prologue."

<tutorial-loot>
source: "Press [F] to loot."
target: "按 [F] 键搜刮战利品。"
type: prompt
status: final
emotion: [mechanical]
context: "Tutorial hint over the first lootable body. The keybind [F] must read exactly as configured by the player."

<combat-log-damage>
source: "{count, plural, one {# point of damage} other {# points of damage}}"
target: "{count, plural, other {# 点伤害}}"
type: sentence
status: final
emotion: [mechanical]
context: "Combat log entry shown each time a hit lands."

<faction-claim>
source: "{faction, select, emberborn {The Emberborn claim your name.} frostward {The Frostward claim your name.} other {No faction claims your name.}}"
target: "{faction, select, emberborn {焰裔承认你的名号。} frostward {霜卫承认你的名号。} other {没有阵营承认你的名号。}}"
type: sentence
status: final
emotion: [mechanical]
context: "Faction choice result shown after the player picks a side at the end of the prologue."

<hit-taken>
source: "You take {damage} damage from the frost."
target: "你受到了来自霜寒的 {damage} 点伤害。"
type: sentence
status: final
emotion: [mechanical]
context: "Floating combat text when the player is hit; {damage} is an engine value that must survive unchanged."

<welcome-name>
source: "Welcome back, {playerName}."
target: "欢迎回来，{playerName}。"
type: sentence
status: final
emotion: [calm]
context: "Main-menu greeting after loading a save; {playerName} is the player's profile name."

<settings-cache>
source: "Clear cache and restore default settings"
target: "清除缓存并恢复默认设置"
type: label
status: final
emotion: [objective]
context: "Button on the system options screen that resets cached data and preferences."

<tutorial-regen>
source: "Drink to restore 40 HP over 10 seconds."
target: "饮用以在 10 秒内恢复 40 HP。"
type: prompt
status: final
emotion: [mechanical]
context: "Tooltip over the tonic's hotbar slot; keep the spacing between Han text and the numbers and Latin letters."

[cutscene.subtitles]
context: "Cutscene subtitles and closed-caption cues for the prologue cinematic. Subtitle lines are timed; keep them within the reading-speed width."

<subtitle-frost>
source: "The frost does not forgive."
target: "霜寒从不宽恕。"
type: subtitle
status: final
emotion: [serious]
max-width: 14
context: "Spoken slowly over roughly three seconds; the width is the reading-speed budget for one subtitle line."

<sfx-ember-crackle>
source: "[Soft ember crackle]"
target: "【余烬轻轻作响】"
type: accessibility-cue
status: final
emotion: [calm]
context: "Closed-caption sound cue for a campfire scene. Style cues in this corner-bracket form."
